From 6ff9931dd828653625500ba61160b10b69ae0fee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Bollerup <mail@r2x2.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:02:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] serve: finished-request sums and finish reasons on /metrics

/metrics adds, over completed generation requests since start, the
count and summed seconds (e2e, queue, ttft, prefill, decode), summed
prompt, cached and output tokens, speculative rounds, drafted and
accepted tokens (ninferno_request_*, ninferno_speculative_*), and
ninferno_requests_finished_total{finish_reason} (stop, length,
tool_calls, abort, repetition; error for failed requests). A scraper
differencing two samples gets each request that finished alone in
between exactly, so a monitor can list every client's requests, as the
NInfer Web UI 0.1.0 Monitor does. The cached tokens are each request's
context-cache hit, which ninferno_reused_prompt_tokens_total leaves out
for a turn resumed from its closure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
